            ; element and the length on every turn, because that is what the
            ; array iterator does. A snapshot taken before the first turn
            ; cannot see `a[1] = 64` written by the body, and misses elements
            ; the body appends.
            ; A Map and a Set are stepped by index for the same reason: their
            ; iterators hold a cursor into the live entry list, so a `set` or a
            ; `delete` the body performs is visible on the next turn. The
            ; snapshot they used to take made `map.set(...)` inside the loop
            ; invisible and kept iterating entries the body had deleted.
