    ; at all, and `new (() => {})` is a TypeError. Minting a prototype on demand
    ; made both answer as if it were an ordinary function. An ASYNC function is
    ; the same: no [[Construct]], no `prototype`. (An async GENERATOR does have
    ; one -- it is what its iterator results inherit from -- so only the plain
    ; async form is suppressed.)
