        ; REFUSES the write. Compiled bodies are only ever sloppy (the compile
        ; gate keeps strict ones on the walker, which owns the TypeError), so
        ; refusing here means dropping the write -- not throwing. Without this
        ; the compiled store went straight into the dense items and
        ; `Object.freeze(a)[0] = 'Z'` took, while the same line at top level
        ; was correctly ignored.
        def peErr:string (this.writeRefusalError(obj pk))
