            ; "function" and the bare-name and Reflect.apply paths both call it,
            ; but here the value is an OBJECT, so it matched no branch and the
            ; call reached "m is not a function" at the end. The RECEIVER is the
            ; object it was read off, which is what the apply trap is handed and
            ; what `this` is when there is no trap.
