        ; built-in stored under another name became callable at all, so the
        ; check has to exist for the borrowing to be modelled honestly.
        ; String.prototype is deliberately absent: those methods coerce their
        ; receiver via ToString and throw only on null/undefined, which the
        ; String block already does.
        if (kind == "number") {
